{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01EcZCXscRPgnYVQpMQ9Ria4","type":"tool_result","content":"1735\t\t// every past closeout stale, without any of them having become less\n1736\t\t// reviewed. This exemption is narrower than legacyPlanExempt: the criteria\n1737\t\t// and tools still stand, only the digest comparison and the class match are\n1738\t\t// waived, and only for a scope already done whose review predates the date.\n1739\t\tvocabularyExempt := s.evidenceVocabularyLegacyExempt(scope, policy, current)\n1740\t\tif vocabularyExempt {\n1741\t\t\teval.Warnings = append(eval.Warnings, \"completed scope retains its approved review recorded before the evidence vocabulary was reconciled\")\n1742\t\t}\n1743\t\t// The same shape again, one contract later. Resolving a criterion's kind put\n1744\t\t// a field into the sealed plan, so every plan digest moved — including those\n1745\t\t// of scopes closed years of commits ago, whose reviews became `superseded`\n1746\t\t// without anything about them having become less reviewed.\n1747\t\t//\n1748\t\t// The spec that introduced the field predicted this and claimed the existing\n1749\t\t// exemption covered completed scopes. It did not: the two above are keyed to\n1750\t\t// their own contracts, and `pose check --strict` failed on the first\n1751\t\t// unrelated done spec it reached. Naming the third one is the fix the\n1752\t\t// pattern already prescribes.\n1753\t\tjudgmentExempt := s.explicitJudgmentLegacyExempt(scope, policy, current)\n1754\t\tif judgmentExempt {\n1755\t\t\teval.Warnings = append(eval.Warnings, \"completed scope retains its approved review recorded before criterion kinds entered the plan\")\n1756\t\t}\n1757\t\tif legacyPlanExempt {\n1758\t\t\trequiredCriteria = append([]ReviewCriterionProfile{}, baseRequiredCriteria...)\n1759\t\t\teffectiveTools = nil\n1760\t\t\tindependence = baseIndependence\n1761\t\t\teval.Warnings = append(eval.Warnings, \"completed scope retains its approved pre-component-aware review attempt\")\n1762\t\t}\n1763\t\tif len(attempts) > 1 && current.Supersedes != attempts[len(attempts)-2].ReviewID {\n1764\t\t\teval.Blockers = append(eval.Blockers, \"latest review does not supersede the previous attempt\")\n1765\t\t}\n1766\t\tif current.ScopeDigest != digest && !legacyPlanExempt {\n1767\t\t\teval.Blockers = append(eval.Blockers, \"review is stale: scope digest changed\")\n1768\t\t} else {\n1769\t\t\teval.Fresh = true\n1770\t\t}\n1771\t\tif eval.PlanDigest != \"\" && current.PlanDigest != eval.PlanDigest && !legacyPlanExempt && !vocabularyExempt && !judgmentExempt {\n1772\t\t\teval.Fresh = false"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"[private-session]","uuid":"80205e80-cda5-46fd-879b-0ada04392d9a","timestamp":"2026-11-27T13:13:56.883Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-review-run-f7649a2054/worktree/pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_closeout.go","content":"\t// every past closeout stale, without any of them having become less\n\t// reviewed. This exemption is narrower than legacyPlanExempt: the criteria\n\t// and tools still stand, only the digest comparison and the class match are\n\t// waived, and only for a scope already done whose review predates the date.\n\tvocabularyExempt := s.evidenceVocabularyLegacyExempt(scope, policy, current)\n\tif vocabularyExempt {\n\t\teval.Warnings = append(eval.Warnings, \"completed scope retains its approved review recorded before the evidence vocabulary was reconciled\")\n\t}\n\t// The same shape again, one contract later. Resolving a criterion's kind put\n\t// a field into the sealed plan, so every plan digest moved — including those\n\t// of scopes closed years of commits ago, whose reviews became `superseded`\n\t// without anything about them having become less reviewed.\n\t//\n\t// The spec that introduced the field predicted this and claimed the existing\n\t// exemption covered completed scopes. It did not: the two above are keyed to\n\t// their own contracts, and `pose check --strict` failed on the first\n\t// unrelated done spec it reached. Naming the third one is the fix the\n\t// pattern already prescribes.\n\tjudgmentExempt := s.explicitJudgmentLegacyExempt(scope, policy, current)\n\tif judgmentExempt {\n\t\teval.Warnings = append(eval.Warnings, \"completed scope retains its approved review recorded before criterion kinds entered the plan\")\n\t}\n\tif legacyPlanExempt {\n\t\trequiredCriteria = append([]ReviewCriterionProfile{}, baseRequiredCriteria...)\n\t\teffectiveTools = nil\n\t\tindependence = baseIndependence\n\t\teval.Warnings = append(eval.Warnings, \"completed scope retains its approved pre-component-aware review attempt\")\n\t}\n\tif len(attempts) > 1 && current.Supersedes != attempts[len(attempts)-2].ReviewID {\n\t\teval.Blockers = append(eval.Blockers, \"latest review does not supersede the previous attempt\")\n\t}\n\tif current.ScopeDigest != digest && !legacyPlanExempt {\n\t\teval.Blockers = append(eval.Blockers, \"review is stale: scope digest changed\")\n\t} else {\n\t\teval.Fresh = true\n\t}\n\tif eval.PlanDigest != \"\" && current.PlanDigest != eval.PlanDigest && !legacyPlanExempt && !vocabularyExempt && !judgmentExempt {\n\t\teval.Fresh = false","numLines":38,"startLine":1735,"totalLines":3019}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01EcZCXscRPgnYVQpMQ9Ria4","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
